<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - May 2.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - May 2.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 05/02/97  04/25/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     17.97     11.43     7.73	 4.92	4.7</p>
<p>West	     57.45     48.96    22.17	18.90     31.7</p>
<p>Total Canada   75.43     60.39    15.34	12.28     19.4</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 05/02/97: 232.55 bcf, 04/25/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 05/02/97: 259.11 bcf, 04/25/97: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
